{"kind":"propose","text":"O1 now has an admitted creation above both example ceilings. The live definition is 202,418 canonical bytes, its accepted genesis is 101,933 bytes, and the tightened meter charges the initial generation 23,217,862 logical bytes. The item has a 100,000-byte type name and 32 unset fixed slots. The actual fixed-index keys repeat that name, even when the fields are empty. The new meter and watch witness passed 44 derive and six native tests. I propose compacting repeated declaration names in the live-only index representation before choosing a ceiling, so existing admitted creation does not become live-unavailable merely because the index repeats names. If you prefer a fixed ceiling with an explicit live-unavailable result above it, please choose that behavior and ceiling policy before activation. The logical charge does not measure heap.","body":{"to":"planner"}}